<p>I see what you mean, but for me it didn't work because it didn't really make me feel anything for the character. I didn't get a sense of him as a person because there's isn't anything from his point of view or direct characterization. Someone telling me how a faceless character was a nice person who died doesn't really evoke any feelings from me and is as effective as just giving me his date of death.</p>
<p>That's why the obit just felt like an explanation for the anomaly, because I didn't feel like there was enough there to incite an empathetic, or even sympathetic, reaction so it just felt like a closing paragraph.</p>
<p>I do like the bit about it being like a Twilight Zone ending, though. I think there's charm in that.</p>

